    "content": "Ethiopian Airlines announced on Wednesday, September 23, 2026, that it has temporarily suspended all flights to the Tigray regional cities of Mekelle, Axum, and Shire. The airline attributed the decision to the prevailing security situation in the region, following reports that the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) has taken control of Mekelle's airport. The suspension affects both domestic and international connections to these destinations.\n\nThe move comes amid heightened tensions in Tigray, where the TPLF's takeover of the airport marks a significant escalation. The airline stated that affected passengers would be notified once flights resume, and expressed regret for the inconvenience caused. Ethiopian Airlines has not provided a specific timeline for the resumption of services.\n\nThe TPLF, which governed Tigray until 2020, has been involved in a prolonged conflict with the federal government. The seizure of the airport in Mekelle, the regional capital, suggests a further consolidation of TPLF control over key infrastructure. This development raises concerns about the stability of the region and the potential for renewed hostilities.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, many of whom rely on Ethiopian Airlines for travel to and from the Horn of Africa, the suspension disrupts vital connections. Ethiopian Airlines is a major carrier for Somali travelers, and the halt in flights to Tigray could complicate travel plans, affect family reunification, and delay the delivery of remittances and humanitarian aid to the region.\n\nThe suspension also highlights the broader risks to regional aviation and trade routes. The Somali diaspora, with strong ties to Ethiopia and the wider region, may face increased travel costs and longer routes as they seek alternative arrangements. Community leaders are urging travelers to stay informed and plan accordingly.\n\nEthiopian Airlines has pledged to keep customers updated on any changes. The situation remains fluid, and further developments are expected. The Somali diaspora is advised to monitor official announcements and exercise caution when traveling in the region.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/23/tplf-la-wareegtay-garoonka-diyaaradaha-ee-mekelle-iyo-duulimaadyadii-oo-hakad-galay/",
